Let $A$ be a finite commutative ring and $p:Z	o T$ a quasi-compact, quasi-separated morphism of schemes. Use constant-$A$ module sheaves on the small etale and pro-etale sites, ordinary derived categories, and exact site comparison $
u_X^*$ [def-weil-pbc-derived-categories, def-weil-pbc-proetale-modules, lem-sf-comparison-pullback-exact]. Write $Q$ for localization of complexes, $a:
u_Z^*p_{\mathrm{et}}^*\simeq p_{\mathrm{proet}}^*
u_T^*$ for the canonical pullback comparison [lem-weil-pbc-comparison-pullback], $d_{p,F}:
u_T^*p_*^{\mathrm{et}}F	o p_*^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_Z^*F$ for the underived counit mate of $a^{-1}$, and $b_{p,K}:
u_T^*Rp_*^{\mathrm{et}}K	o Rp_*^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_Z^*K$ for its specified derived counit mate [def-weil-pbc-adjunction-mate, lem-weil-pbc-comparison-direct-image-canonical-mate]. For every bounded-below complex $P$ on $Z_{\mathrm{et}}$, let
$$\gamma_P^{\mathrm{et}}:Q(p_*^{\mathrm{et}}P)	o Rp_*^{\mathrm{et}}QP,\qquad \gamma_{
u_Z^*P}^{\mathrm{proet}}:Q(p_*^{\mathrm{proet}}
u_Z^*P)	o Rp_*^{\mathrm{proet}}Q
u_Z^*P$$
be the canonical right-derived comparison maps. Then
$$b_{p,QP}
u_T^*(\gamma_P^{\mathrm{et}})=\gamma_{
u_Z^*P}^{\mathrm{proet}}Q(d_{p,P}).$$
More precisely the two sides have the same adjoint transpose, namely both $
u_Z^*Q(\varepsilon_P^{0,\mathrm{et}})a^{-1}$ and $Q(\varepsilon_{
u_Z^*P}^{0,\mathrm{proet}}p_{\mathrm{proet}}^*(d_{p,P}))$, where $\varepsilon^{0,s}$ are the termwise ordinary counits. In particular, suppose $e:U	o T$ is separated etale of finite type, $e=pj$ is a compactification with quasi-compact open $j:U\hookrightarrow Z$ and proper $p$, and $G^s,\sigma,o$ are the graph sheaf maps, the adjunction-preserving sum-extension site isomorphism, and the open site isomorphism specified in [lem-sp-et-proet-graph-sheaf-square]. Set $\Theta^s=\gamma^sQ(G^s)$ on complexes. For every bounded-below complex $K$ on $U_{\mathrm{et}}$, with $P=j_!^{\mathrm{et}}K$, one has
$$\Theta^{\mathrm{proet}}(
u_U^*QK)\sigma_{QK}=Rp_*^{\mathrm{proet}}(o_{QK})\gamma_{
u_Z^*P}^{\mathrm{proet}}Q(d_{p,P})
u_T^*Q(G_K^{\mathrm{et}})=Rp_*^{\mathrm{proet}}(o_{QK})b_{p,QP}
u_T^*(\Theta^{\mathrm{et}}(QK)).$$
The representative compatibility is natural in bounded-below complexes $P$; the compactified graph chain is an identity of natural transformations on $D^+(U_{\mathrm{et}},A)$. No preservation of injectives by $
u^*$ or invertibility of $\gamma$ is assumed.
